  "_comment": "Single source of truth for idiomorph and MAT gene labels (curator rulings 2026-10-28, see docs/notes/2026-10-28_idiomorph-naming-proposal.md). Grammar <Lineage>__<System>_<Cell>; system = frozen code of the reference organism; labels are computed on output from (family_called, raw name) and are never stored in records. A family with system null has no approved system code yet: its raw names are returned unchanged. Basidiomycota (multiallelic systems): a family with `locus` is labelled <Lineage>__<System>_<Locus>[-<Allele>]; the allele is the raw idiomorph (A1, b1, v2 ...) and is left out when it is undetermined. A family with `cells` and no `locus` (Cryptococcus MAT) uses the cell token. registry_version = registry_date + registry_hash (first 8 hex of the SHA-256 of the canonical registry without _comment and registry_hash): bump registry_date by hand when a rule change is approved, then run `python3 scripts/idiomorph_labels.py --stamp`; the tests fail if the hash is stale. frozen_codes lists the approved lineage and system codes: a code may not be removed or renamed; a rename needs an entry in aliases (old -> new) and a deprecation note here. A code is added to frozen_codes when the curator approves it (PicKud approved 2026-10-29).",
